        <h1>Top Cloud Computing Certifications in 2026: AWS, Azure and Google Cloud</h1>

        <p class="intro">
            Cloud computing has become an essential part of modern businesses.
            Organisations use cloud platforms to host applications, store data,
            improve security, scale digital services and support artificial
            intelligence workloads. Learning cloud computing can help students
            and IT professionals explore new opportunities in the technology industry.
        </p>

        <p>
            At Global SkillTech Pvt. Ltd., learners can explore IT skills that
            support cloud computing, including networking, Linux, Windows Server,
            cybersecurity and cloud fundamentals. Combining these skills with
            hands-on projects and a suitable certification path can help you
            prepare for cloud-related career opportunities.
        </p>

        <h2>Why Are Cloud Computing Certifications Important?</h2>

        <p>
            Cloud certifications provide a structured way to learn cloud
            technologies and demonstrate knowledge of a particular platform.
            They can help learners understand cloud infrastructure, networking,
            storage, identity management, monitoring and security.
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>Develop a structured understanding of cloud computing.</li>
            <li>Learn about cloud services and infrastructure management.</li>
            <li>Build practical skills through labs and projects.</li>
            <li>Prepare for relevant technical interviews.</li>
            <li>Explore career paths in cloud administration, engineering and DevOps.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="highlight">
            <strong>Important:</strong> A certification alone does not guarantee
            employment or a particular salary. Practical experience, technical
            skills and problem-solving ability are also important.
        </div>

        <h2>Top Global Cloud Computing Certifications</h2>

        <h3>1. Amazon Web Services (AWS) Certifications</h3>

        <p>
            Amazon Web Services (AWS) provides cloud services for computing,
            storage, databases, networking, security and application deployment.
            AWS certifications cover different levels of knowledge and job roles.
        </p>

        <p><strong>Popular certification options:</strong></p>

        <ul>
            <li>AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner</li>
            <li>AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Associate</li>
            <li>AWS Certified Developer – Associate</li>
            <li>AWS Certified SysOps Administrator – Associate</li>
            <li>Advanced AWS certifications for experienced professionals</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Potential career paths:</strong></p>

        <ul>
            <li>AWS Cloud Engineer</li>
            <li>Cloud Support Associate</li>
            <li>Solutions Architect</li>
            <li>DevOps Engineer</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2. Microsoft Azure Certifications</h3>

        <p>
            Microsoft Azure is a cloud computing platform used for application
            hosting, virtual machines, networking, storage, databases and
            enterprise services. Azure knowledge can be particularly useful
            alongside Windows Server, Microsoft 365 and identity management skills.
        </p>

        <p><strong>Popular certification options:</strong></p>

        <ul>
            <li>AZ-900: Microsoft Azure Fundamentals</li>
            <li>AZ-104: Microsoft Azure Administrator</li>
            <li>AZ-305: Designing Microsoft Azure Infrastructure Solutions</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Potential career paths:</strong></p>

        <ul>
            <li>Azure Administrator</li>
            <li>Cloud Support Engineer</li>
            <li>Cloud Consultant</li>
            <li>Cloud Solutions Architect</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>3. Google Cloud Certifications</h3>

        <p>
            Google Cloud offers cloud infrastructure, data analytics,
            application development and AI-related services. Its certification
            paths can help learners build skills for cloud engineering,
            architecture and data-focused roles.
        </p>

        <p><strong>Popular certification options:</strong></p>

        <ul>
            <li>Associate Cloud Engineer</li>
            <li>Professional Cloud Architect</li>
            <li>Professional Data Engineer</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Potential career paths:</strong></p>

        <ul>
            <li>Cloud Engineer</li>
            <li>Cloud Architect</li>
            <li>Data Engineer</li>
            <li>Cloud Developer</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>4. CompTIA Cloud+</h3>

        <p>
            CompTIA Cloud+ is a vendor-neutral certification focused on
            cloud infrastructure operations. It covers concepts that can
            apply across cloud and hybrid environments.
        </p>

        <p><strong>Key learning areas include:</strong></p>

        <ul>
            <li>Cloud infrastructure and architecture</li>
            <li>Cloud deployment and operations</li>
            <li>Monitoring and troubleshooting</li>
            <li>Cloud security and resource management</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Potential career paths:</strong> Cloud Support Technician,
        Systems Administrator and Infrastructure Support Engineer.</p>

        <h3>5. IBM and Oracle Cloud Certifications</h3>

        <p>
            IBM and Oracle offer learning and certification options related
            to enterprise cloud services, databases, infrastructure and
            business applications. The best option depends on the technologies
            used in your target organisation.
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>Explore relevant IBM cloud and enterprise technology paths.</li>
            <li>Explore Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI) certifications.</li>
            <li>Build database, infrastructure and cloud administration skills.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Cloud Computing Career Opportunities</h2>

        <p>
            Cloud computing skills can be relevant to several IT career paths.
            The responsibilities and requirements vary by employer and experience level.
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li><strong>Cloud Support Engineer:</strong> Troubleshoot cloud services and user issues.</li>
            <li><strong>Cloud Administrator:</strong> Manage cloud resources, access and monitoring.</li>
            <li><strong>Cloud Engineer:</strong> Deploy and maintain cloud infrastructure.</li>
            <li><strong>Cloud Architect:</strong> Design secure, reliable and scalable cloud solutions.</li>
            <li><strong>DevOps Engineer:</strong> Improve software delivery through automation and deployment tools.</li>
            <li><strong>Cloud Security Engineer:</strong> Help protect cloud systems, identities and data.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Cloud Computing Salary in India</h2>

        <p>
            Salaries for cloud-related jobs depend on experience, location,
            technical expertise, employer and job responsibilities. Entry-level
            support roles may have different salary ranges from experienced
            cloud engineers, architects and security specialists.
        </p>

        <p>
            Before making a career decision, research current job listings
            for your target role and experience level. Focus on the skills
            employers request, such as Linux, networking, scripting,
            automation, cloud security and infrastructure management.
        </p>

        <h2>How to Choose the Right Cloud Certification</h2>

        <h3>Step 1: Learn IT Fundamentals</h3>

        <p>
            Beginners should develop a foundation in computer hardware,
            networking, operating systems, Linux and basic cybersecurity
            before moving to more advanced cloud topics.
        </p>

        <h3>Step 2: Choose Your Cloud Platform</h3>

        <p>
            AWS, Azure and Google Cloud are useful options. Choose a platform
            based on your interests, learning goals and the requirements
            of jobs you want to pursue.
        </p>

        <h3>Step 3: Practise with Cloud Labs</h3>

        <p>
            Practise deploying virtual machines, configuring networks,
            managing storage, setting access permissions and monitoring
            cloud resources. Check provider pricing and clean up resources
            to avoid unexpected charges.
        </p>

        <h3>Step 4: Build Practical Projects</h3>

        <p>
            Create projects such as hosting a website, configuring a virtual
            network, setting up monitoring or documenting a secure cloud
            architecture. Practical projects help demonstrate what you have learned.
        </p>

        <h3>Step 5: Prepare for Your Certification Exam</h3>

        <p>
            Review the official exam guide, practise relevant questions
            and verify the current exam name, syllabus, fee and requirements
            on the certification provider's website.
        </p>

