        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <h3>Which cloud certification is best for beginners?</h3>

        <p>
            AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner and Microsoft Azure Fundamentals
            (AZ-900) are common starting points. Choose according to your
            interests and learning goals.
        </p>

        <h3>Can I learn cloud computing without coding?</h3>

        <p>
            Yes. You can begin with cloud fundamentals and administration.
            Learning basic scripting later can help you automate tasks and
            expand your technical skills.
        </p>

        <h3>Does a cloud certification guarantee a job?</h3>

        <p>
            No certification guarantees employment. Employers also consider
            practical skills, projects, communication and relevant experience.
        </p>

        <h3>Should I learn AWS or Azure first?</h3>

        <p>
            Both are useful options. Consider the types of roles you want,
            the technologies used by target employers and the learning
            resources available to you.
        </p>

